Subject: VmsCommandLauncher: quote arguments, run Unix paths, return Unix exit codes

The DCL script wrote each argument unquoted, so DCL split it at spaces and
upper-cased it under the TRADITIONAL parse style, and a DEFINE value with a
quote broke. Arguments with white space or ! are now quoted; others are
left alone, so DCL qualifiers (/SIZE) still work, and so is an argument
that has a double quote already, which is taken to be written for DCL (<arg
value='"Two words"'/>). DEFINE values are always quoted, and the script
sets the EXTENDED parse style. A command given as an absolute Unix path
(DCL's %DCL-W-NOCOMD) is run as a foreign command or with @. The script
returns a success status as EXIT 1, which VSI's JVM reports as 0 (patch
0003). Starting a DCL procedure straight from VSI's JVM fails at random
(%DCL-E-OPENIN on its input mailbox, 9 times in 15), so if
ant.openvms.dclrunner names an image (the port's ANTDCL.EXE), the script is
run through it. NOTES N6, N8.

--- a/vmsport/src/ant/org/apache/tools/ant/taskdefs/launcher/VmsCommandLauncher.java
+++ b/vmsport/src/ant/org/apache/tools/ant/taskdefs/launcher/VmsCommandLauncher.java
