  * A command launcher for VMS that writes the command to a temporary
  * DCL script before launching commands. This is due to limitations of
  * both the DCL interpreter and the Java VM implementation.
+ *
+ * <p>The script quotes the arguments that DCL would split or cut short
+ * (white space, an exclamation mark), and sets the EXTENDED parse style, so
+ * a program gets its arguments as given; others are left as they are, so
+ * that DCL qualifiers such as /SIZE still work, and so is one that has a
+ * double quote, which is taken to be written for DCL already. A command
+ * given as an absolute Unix path is run as a foreign command (an image) or
+ * with @ (a .COM procedure).</p>
+ *
+ * <p>If the system property <code>ant.openvms.dclrunner</code> names an
+ * image, the script is run through it ("runner script"): starting a DCL
+ * procedure directly from VSI's JVM fails at random with %DCL-E-OPENIN on
+ * its input mailbox. The runner returns a Unix exit code: 0 for a success
+ * status. Without one the script ends with EXIT 1 for success, which VSI's
+ * JVM reports as 0, and the status otherwise.</p>
  */
 public class VmsCommandLauncher extends Java13CommandLauncher {
 
